James sought advice on reheating take-home ramen that had its soup separate from the noodles and veggies. I suggested a method to maintain the freshness of each component: heat the soup on the stove or in the microwave while stirring, and briefly blanch the noodles and veggies in boiling water or microwave them with added water in short intervals. Once warmed, he could combine all ingredients for an enjoyable meal, preserving the noodles' texture and the veggies' crunch.
